{"chunks":[{"id":"chunk-1","nodes":["inline","path:1","path:2","path:3","path:4","path:5"],"sha256":"sha256-SgFj8EE6PptJzCCxkBaHOsC1zBGtPmvyGmWfdBuiF5M"}],"loss":[],"mode":"semantic","nodes":[{"attrs":{"level":"1"},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"inline","path":"0","sha256":"sha256-mpLkTobU-5kGZL3UXQSVtayDvpSJmoqKR4UEi35DQDk","text":"Inline extensions","type":"heading"},{"attrs":{},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"","path":"1","sha256":"sha256-nRrF-QETCtjWh0TWGVcTGWidrGVs5sdZeO7gEGjkLtU","text":"Underscore emphasis applies at word boundaries: em and strong work\njust like em and strong.","type":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"","path":"2","sha256":"sha256-Oo0lqHtc8BW69h6Og4CNmf4cuaV9f-HG1PTvhAKgyHI","text":"Intraword underscores stay literal because the run is flanked by\nalphanumerics on both sides. Examples: snake_case identifiers, my_var_name\nreferences, and snake__case patterns are preserved as plain text.","type":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"","path":"3","sha256":"sha256-bDDOgozuTjAEpDP9DqDaQyyJrbAKkyQk6bj92WZ4pTQ","text":"Code spans support runs of one, two, or three backticks: single, two ` ticks,\nand three backticks `` two `` runs inside.","type":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"","path":"4","sha256":"sha256-oMiGrD63tAETWfDhxewkwnfSPAUO2VdX-R73EwYvMOk","text":"Backslash escapes the extended set: _underscore_, !bang, .dot, -dash,\n+plus, <less, >greater, \\backslash, \"quote\", 'apos'.","type":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{},"children":[],"classes":[],"id":"","path":"5","sha256":"sha256-E-IURsTPqPfnidcXcdjFf2FfRDnPMqZlxV-VHczAp2k","text":"Hard line break with backslash: first half second half on the next line.","type":"paragraph"}],"schema":"nodx-ncp/1.0","sourceHash":"sha256-n5Nm9akUjSl-vSXe5hH6AFON-arFSdisdQkqhQfCPyU"}
